### Nomos - Ad-hoc Rule Management
### Use these to add rules to an existing graph

### ============================================================
### Add a new rule to billing-service for auth0
### ============================================================

### Rule: validate country + msisdn on billing invoices path
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/admin/rule
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "proxyName": "billing-service",
  "idpName": "auth0",
  "pathPattern": "/{country}/billing/{msisdn}/invoices",
  "methods": ["GET"],
  "validations": [
    {
      "order": 1,
      "level": 1,
      "paramName": "country",
      "jwtJsonPath": "$.country",
      "validation": "equals"
    },
    {
      "order": 2,
      "level": 2,
      "paramName": "msisdn",
      "jwtJsonPath": "$.aL",
      "validation": "contains"
    }
  ]
}

### ============================================================
### Add a rule with enrichment to payment-gateway for keycloak
### ============================================================

### Rule: validate country + accountId, with enrichment when JWT is incomplete
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/admin/rule
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "proxyName": "payment-gateway",
  "idpName": "keycloak",
  "pathPattern": "/{country}/payments/{accountId}/transfer",
  "methods": ["POST"],
  "validations": [
    {
      "order": 1,
      "level": 1,
      "paramName": "country",
      "jwtJsonPath": "$.realm_access.country",
      "validation": "equals"
    },
    {
      "order": 2,
      "level": 2,
      "paramName": "accountId",
      "jwtJsonPath": "$.realm_access.accounts",
      "validation": "contains",
      "enrichment": {
        "conditionJsonPath": "$.realm_access.allAccounts",
        "conditionEquals": false,
        "endpoint": "/users/me/accounts",
        "domainFrom": "jwtIssuer",
        "responseJsonPath": "$.accounts[*].id",
        "cacheTtlSeconds": 600
      }
    }
  ]
}

### ============================================================
### Add a simple rule (no enrichment) to notification-service for cognito
### ============================================================

### Rule: only validate country (level 1 only, no personification)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/admin/rule
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "proxyName": "notification-service",
  "idpName": "cognito",
  "pathPattern": "/{country}/notifications/send",
  "methods": ["POST"],
  "validations": [
    {
      "order": 1,
      "level": 1,
      "paramName": "country",
      "jwtJsonPath": "$.custom:country",
      "validation": "equals"
    }
  ]
}

### ============================================================
### Verify: get rules for billing-service + auth0 audience
### ============================================================

### Should return the rule we just created
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/rules?proxy=billing-service&aud=mobile-br-auth0-client&iss=https%3A%2F%2Fauth0.example.com&method=GET
